WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.240
Let’s say you’ve given up your law-abiding
lifestyle to pursue a life of crime- you’ve

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.730
just made your first big score, perhaps from
selling drugs, taking a bribe, or other corrupt

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:11.730
acts.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.009
you can't just spend it or deposit it in
your bank account without attracting

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:17.020
attention from authorities.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.090
That pesky
money trail might serve as evidence of

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.090
the crime you committed.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.980
So you need to
get that dirty money clean.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:24.980
There are

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.850
three steps to any money laundering
scheme.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:27.850
First up,

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.340
placement, where funds are moved from
direct association with the crime, then,

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.450
layering or disguising the money trail
to foil any authorities, and finally,

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.970
integration, where the funds are once
again available to spend without worry

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.430
of being caught.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.160
So what are your options?

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.510
One option is forming a shell company.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.710
It's fairly easy and there are plenty of
law firms who can help.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.710
It should take

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.900
them only a bit longer than signing up
for a new email address.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.370
Launderers may turn to historic tax havens
like Switzerland, or places where

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.760
you can set up anonymous shell companies like
the Cayman Islands or the U.S. states of Delaware

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.820
and Nevada.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.390
Once a shell company is established,

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:05.840
make up some fake transactions for
goods or services that you pay for with

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.150
your dirty money.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.799
Suddenly that dirty
money looks legitimate.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:10.799
It also helps to

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:13.140
find people who work in
banking who don't care if you're a shady

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.140
client.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.500
After the fall of the Soviet
Union launderers sought out weak spots

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.300
throughout Europe where oversight was
poor.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.549
Billions have been funneled through

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:26.280
banks in Cyprus, Malta and the Baltic
nations of Estonia and Latvia

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.750
If you prefer to use the stock market
you can try a technique called mirror

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:30.930
trading.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.850
In this method you use your
money to purchase shares.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:34.850
And then you

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.049
sell shares worth the same amount
somewhere abroad.

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:40.220
The trades functionally cancel each
other out,

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.869
but you've successfully turned your

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:44.450
rubles into clean euros.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.390
A similar
method is a back-to-back deal, where, say,

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:52.110
a Russian takes out a loan in one country,
say Austria, that's guaranteed by a deposit

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.120
of dirty money back home in Russia.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.340
She then defaults on the loan, the bank in
Austria seizes the Russian deposit, but she

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:02.690
still ends up with the proceeds of the loan,
no strings attached.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:03.969
Or maybe you like to visit

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:04.969
casinos.

00:02:04.969 --> 00:02:07.280
Another method of money
laundering is mixing dirty money in with

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.479
clean.

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:11.510
Cash businesses like restaurants
and casinos are particularly attractive

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:12.510
to launderers.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:16.010
A common scheme is to buy
a bunch of casino chips, make a few small

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.330
wagers, then cash everything else out as
winnings.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:21.330
Or, you can just own the whole

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.330
casino.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.330
Macau has been beset by
laundering schemes despite China's

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.330
repeated attempts to stop it.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.330
Or finally,
there's smurfing- though you won't need

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.330
anything blue to get your green.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.080
With
this one you hire a bunch of associates

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.510
called Smurfs to individually deposit
small chunks of the large haul you're

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.930
trying to cleanse, in different accounts,
in different places.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:36.930
Beware!

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:41.260
US banks are required to report
any transaction over $10,000, so you

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.569
might need to find a lot of Smurfs.

00:02:44.569 --> 00:02:46.569
So
you can see there are lots of ways to

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:47.569
launder money.

00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:50.810
Unfortunately for you, there’s no guarantee
that you won’t get caught.

